// PricingRule How a dub or segment generation is priced: `max(1, round(s/60))` minutes (half to even) over the speech seconds `s` below; a free dubbing variant costs 0. Speech seconds read each segment's interval, so `createDub`, `generateSegments` and a run's dub answer 422 `validation_failed` (`errors[].code: text_too_long_for_interval`) on a translation above 60 characters per second of its interval, or 100 on any interval. When every line passes, all one request voices may hold at most 3600 characters for each minute its speech is priced at, the list price also for a free dubbing variant: above that it answers 422 `validation_failed` (`errors[].code: text_too_long_for_price`, pointer `/segment_ids` or `/segments`).
//
// - `full`: speech seconds of every segment (auto-dub: the processed media duration)
// - `changed_speech`: speech seconds of the voiced segments, with no cap at the full price
// - `selected_speech`: speech seconds of the chosen segments (segment generation)
// - `free_language`: free dubbing variant
type PricingRule string

