	// Voices the chosen segments (1-100) into one downloadable `SegmentClip` per segment, without rebuilding the video: a take stored under the job and never overwritten, at its natural duration (`fit`, `overrun_seconds`); any voiced clip counts as success. Text is voiced as written.
	//
	// **When to use:** to download or check chosen lines before a dub. A later `changed_segments` dub merges unchanged clips without charging them again (estimateDub lists them). A first or full dub voices and charges every segment; when only reused segments changed, the shortest is voiced again at its own speech price (minimum 1 minute).
	//
	// **Side effects:** Segments are `voicing` until the job ends; then `audio` is the new take and `dub_state` is `outdated` (`not_dubbed` without a dub), or the previous state on failure. ETags may change on any take: use `clips[].segment_etag`, or re-read before an edit.
	//
	// **Cost:** Spends `max(1, round(s/60))` minutes (half to even), with `s` the speech seconds of the chosen segments; a free dubbing variant costs 0. Pass estimateSegmentGeneration's `total_minutes` as `expected_cost_minutes`. If a segment fails, the job fails and refunds whole, usually with no clips; retry with a new key.
	//
	// **Async:** returns `202` and a `segment_generation` Job (`Location`); wait with `GET /v3/jobs/{job_id}?wait_seconds=20` (poll hint 5 s); typically 30 s (p95 5 min).
