// Starts a `dub` job: `full` re-voices every segment, `changed_segments` only outdated and not-dubbed ones, `auto` (default) picks full without a previous dub or when a full voiceover is needed. Text is voiced as written. A `changed_segments` dub merges unchanged clips from generateSegments without voicing or charging them again (estimateDub); if all changed segments have one, the shortest is voiced again at its speech price (minimum 1 minute). A first or full dub voices every segment. The video and outputs are rebuilt and a `dub_completed` version is recorded; segments edited during the dub stay `outdated`.
//
// **When to use:** after edits or voice changes, after generateSegments, or for a first dub after a skipped auto-dub: its charge opens the text.
//
// **Side effects:** Creates a dub job. v3 refuses a dub during a lip-sync on any channel.
//
// **Cost:** Spends `max(1, round(s/60))` minutes (half to even), `s` = speech seconds voiced (every segment for `full`); free dubbing variants cost 0. Pass estimateDub's `total_minutes` as `expected_cost_minutes`. A failed dub refunds its minutes, and the project's first voiceover or merge failure also refunds its project credit (unless unlimited).
//
// **Async:** returns `202` and a `dub` Job (`Location`); wait with getJob `wait_seconds=20` (poll hint 10 s); typically 5 min (p95 30 min).
//
